-// Build-time source-content sha12 for the binary_sha12 field. Defined at
-// compile time via -DDOSKUTSU_BUILD_SHA12=<git-short-sha> from the
-// top-level Makefile. The Makefile passes it as a bare token (no
-// quotes); C preprocessor stringify converts to "literal" at compile
-// time. Avoids the multi-layer quote-escape pain through bash + make
-// + cmake -> compiler -D forwarding.
+// Build-CONTENT fingerprint for the binary_sha12 manifest field:
+// sha256[:12] over the repo HEAD commit sha + the concatenated contents
+// of all applied patches/**/*.patch (build-qa #19 Makefile fix). Passed
+// at compile time via -DDOSKUTSU_BUILD_SHA12=<fingerprint> from the top-
+// level Makefile. Unlike the pre-#19 `git rev-parse HEAD` alone (a
+// commit base-pin that collided with a commit sha AND did NOT change
+// when the working tree had uncommitted patches), this fingerprint
+// CHANGES with the applied-patch set -- so a v1.0.4 build (base +
+// uncommitted v1.0.4 patches) gets a value distinct from the v1.0.3
+// commit sha. NOTE: it is a SOURCE-INPUT fingerprint (HEAD + patch
+// text), NOT the literal exe-content hash (build-qa's deferred follow-
+// up). The Makefile passes it as a bare token (no quotes); C
+// preprocessor stringify converts to "literal" at compile time.
 // Fallback "UNKNOWN_____" (12 chars; pads the sha12 field) if the
 // Makefile didn't pass the define (e.g., out-of-tree CMake build).
 #define _DOSKUTSU_STRINGIFY(x) #x
